      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Heparin is considered necessary during percutaneous coronary interventions; however, heparin is contraindicated in patients with heparin-induced thrombocytopenia and/or heparin antibodies. We describe the successful use of the heparinoid Orgaran (danaparoid sodium) in addition to abciximab (ReoPro) in a patient with heparin antibodies who required rotational atherectomy."},
